--- a mistake no argument can fix, at the trace
--- the same mistake, found by a definition check
--- an argument the scheme refuses, at the application
--- a nested layer refusing a closed feature size: the outer function is named
--- the same layer under an opted-out function: the layer is named
--- an argument with too few axes for the spec
--- a dimension and a row variable sharing a name
--- an empty concatenation component
--- undetermined concatenation components, at the closure (a variable in the message)
--- a failed total-elements constraint (hand-built: the solver raises it on divisibility)
--- the first mistake without a scheme (session ids, for contrast)
every case raised a shape error: true
every application error names the scheme that refused it: true
the raw constraint sexp of an error in a scheme spells a reserved-range id: true
with shape_error_full_sexp, a printed error in a scheme spells a reserved-range id: true
with shape_error_full_sexp, the exception's sexp is the raw one: true
every scheme error lists the origins naming the scheme's tensors first: true
no error holds more origins than the cap: true
some scheme error's origins name both the scheme's tensors and others: true
